Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["player absence", "offensive reorganization relative to baseline L", "change in points per possession (PPP)", "lineup and rotation disruption", "play-type possession records"],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "How is offensive reorganization relative to L defined and measured, and is L specified before the outcome is observed?",
  "Is the unit of analysis the spell (n=148) or the possession (n=986), and are possessions nested within spells and players?",
  "What minimum detectable effect (rho) does the stated design target, and does n=148 reach it?",
  "Can reorganization be separated from regression to the mean and from absence-context confounding?",
  "Are player-level PPP and play-type labels complete enough in the graph to score the outcome?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF20",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Pre-registered test on 23 player-season absences from 18 franchises. V1 (real absence moves the association structure) was confirmed (16/23 above own-null p95, binomial p=2.67e-16; V1(b) +0.142, CI [+0.103, +0.187]). V2 (simulation predicts magnitude) was not confirmed (V2a rho +0.288, p=0.077, CI [-0.244, +0.667]; V2b partial +0.253, p=0.115). Franchises were below the registered floor of about 20. One record notes a later full-pool run reversed V2. The record's limit is small_sample."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF04",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Live suppression-trigger timing in playoff replays (101 to 228 triggers, 100% actionable). Tier vs ROG PPP was not significant (rho -0.0457, p=0.456, n=268). BEST vs AVOID p=0.073965 in the 10-series replay, and the record says it was confirmed in the 25-series replay. The early-vs-late gap (0.701 vs 0.415) rests on 26 early triggers. One record calls its p=0.031 (n=57) weak evidence."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF31",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Scan of 6,221 (offense, opponent, play type) cells for head-to-head leaders. The apparent edge (+1.26 PPP at n>=5, +1.13 at n>=15) came from low-n cells, typically 1-shot role players at 3.00 PPP. The record attributes the edge to small-sample inflation and recommends keeping the n>=15 gate."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-009",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Compared V4 and V5 player routing on observed PPP. Of 8 divergences, 0 were scoreable: players were missing from Neo4j and V5 mostly routed to 'team'. The record notes data coverage could be checked before running. Recorded failure type A_unanswerable."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF20",
   "what_failed": "Magnitude test (V2) of an absence-simulation prediction on a pool of 23 absences across 18 franchises, with a registered floor of about 20 per franchise.",
   "why": "Recorded limitation LIM:small_sample. The CI spans from -0.244 to +0.667, so the test was too imprecise to support or reject the magnitude claim. A later full-pool run reversed V2."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF31",
   "what_failed": "Routing signal estimated from head-to-head cells with few possessions (n>=5 gate).",
   "why": "Recorded as small-sample distortion: leaders were role players on 5-7 possessions, so the apparent PPP edge was an artifact (C_artifact). The n>=15 gate reduced but did not remove the inflation (+1.13)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-009",
   "what_failed": "Player-level PPP comparison of routing rules from the graph.",
   "why": "Recorded as A_unanswerable: players were missing from Neo4j, so no divergence was scoreable (0 of 8)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF04",
   "what_failed": "Early-vs-late trigger timing comparison, and a tier-PPP correlation.",
   "why": "Recorded as inconclusive: the early-trigger subset had 26 cases, the BEST vs AVOID p-value sat near 0.05 (0.074 in one replay), and the tier correlation was null."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Earlier studies in this project that were retrieved have small effective samples (23 absences; 26 early triggers; 8 divergences). Several were recorded as underpowered, untestable, or artifactual.",
  "Subset and gate choices in earlier analyses inflated apparent PPP effects when cells had few possessions (FAM:SF31).",
  "Missing player coverage in the graph blocked player-level PPP scoring in an earlier study (FAM:SF-APPS-009). This is a concrete data-coverage risk for the present question's outcome."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "No retrieved record tests whether offensive reorganization relative to L predicts change in PPP. None of the four records studies reorganization, change in PPP after absence, or the L baseline.",
  "No retrieved record gives a power calculation or realized MDE for the present n=148 spell design.",
  "The retrieved records do not show whether reorganization is reliable across games or seasons.",
  "No record defines L."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The retrieved records concern adjacent questions (absence structure, trigger timing, routing), so they inform design risks but do not answer the question.",
  "Under a simple correlation with two-sided alpha 0.05, n=148 independent spells gives roughly 80% power only for |rho| near 0.23. Modest effects are underpowered, and the power estimate falls if spells cluster within players or teams.",
  "The n=986 possession count is not a valid independent sample size, since possessions share spells, players, and games."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "L is not defined anywhere in the task, so the exposure cannot be specified.",
  "The 'MDE rho' value is unstated, and it is unclear whether n=148 or n=986 is the analysis unit.",
  "Regular-season 2025-26 is complete only from 2026-04-13, and playoffs only from 2026-06-21. The 2026-11-01 data cut has partial 2025-26 data, so the sample may shift.",
  "Whether the graph contains the players needed to score PPP for each spell is unverified.",
  "Full text of several records was truncated ('read_family for the full text'). The statuses and figures above are as far as the retrieved excerpts go."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "Retrieved evidence showed that earlier studies in this project were underpowered (SF20, SF04), produced small-sample artifacts (SF31), and failed on player-level coverage (SF-APPS-009). These findings moved the decision from a straightforward test to do_not_proceed as posed, until L, the unit, the MDE, and graph coverage are specified."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.35,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "Player-level PPP may be missing from the graph (SF-APPS-009). Spell-level outcome completeness has not been verified."},
   {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "n=148 spells gives adequate power only for moderate-to-large |rho|. The stated MDE is unspecified, and the unit (spell vs possession) is ambiguous."},
   {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "'Reorganization relative to L' is undefined, and its test-retest reliability is unknown."}
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "no",
  "cited": ["FAM:SF20", "FAM:SF04", "FAM:SF31", "FAM:SF-APPS-009"],
  "summary": "None of the retrieved records tests reorganization relative to L predicting change in PPP after absence. The cited records are related in method and data (absence structure, small-sample gates, graph coverage) and are used only to identify risks."
 },
 "risks": [
  {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "At n=148 spells, power is adequate only for moderate effects. Earlier records show small-n inflation (SF31) and underpowered magnitude tests (SF20)."},
  {"code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL", "text": "Change in PPP is derived from play-by-play and the graph, so the outcome depends on how possessions and points are attributed."},
  {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "Missing players in the graph caused outcomes to go unscored in SF-APPS-009."},
  {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "Reorganization relative to L needs test-retest reliability before it can serve as an exposure."},
  {"code": "RTM_SELECTION", "text": "Absences are selected (for example injuries after high or low performance). Change in PPP can regress to the mean."},
  {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Absence type, minutes, opponent, and season context can drive both reorganization and PPP change."},
  {"code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD", "text": "If L or the reorganization measure uses post-absence data, the test leaks the outcome."},
  {"code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY", "text": "Few spells per player or team limit the within-unit contrasts and the stability of estimates."},
  {"code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING", "text": "Multiple L definitions, windows, or subsets invite selective reporting (as in SF04's early subset)."},
  {"code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY", "text": "Scoring and play styles shift across 2022-23 to 2025-26, and 2025-26 is partial at the data cut."}
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.2,
  "rejected": 0.15,
  "untestable": 0.3,
  "artifact": 0.15,
  "uncertain": 0.2
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Within-spell association between standardized offensive reorganization relative to a pre-registered baseline L and the change in PPP following a player absence (regression slope and Spearman rho with 95% CI).",
  "unit": "Player absence spell (n=148 as the primary unit). Possessions are aggregated to spell level; the 986 possession count is secondary and not used for inference.",
  "sample": "Regular-season spells from 2022-23 to 2024-25 (complete), plus 2025-26 regular season only after its completion date. Playoffs excluded from the primary test. Freeze the dataset and the spell list before analysis.",
  "power": "Pre-register the MDE at 80% power, alpha 0.05, and cluster-adjusted n. For n=148 independent spells, the MDE is roughly |rho| 0.23. If clustering by player reduces effective n, state the reduced MDE and do not run the test if it exceeds the effect of interest.",
  "controls": "Pre-absence baseline PPP and reorganization, minutes and usage of the absent player, absence type, opponent strength, season fixed effects, and cluster-robust SEs by player and team. Define L before outcome data are accessed. Verify graph coverage of all spell players first, and report any unscored spells.",
  "falsification": "Placebo windows with no absence (same players, matched games). Reorganization should not predict PPP change in placebo windows. A negative control outcome (for example, PPP change for the non-absent teammates) should show no association.",
  "multiplicity": "One primary test (spell-level slope at the pre-registered L). Secondary analyses (alternative L, playoff subset, possession-level models) are exploratory and corrected with Holm.",
  "decision_rule": "Supported only if the primary 95% CI excludes zero, the placebo and negative-control associations are null, and the result holds after controls and cluster adjustment. Rejected only if the design reaches the pre-registered MDE and the CI is within the null range. Otherwise uncertain. Report artifacts if the effect disappears under the n>=15-type gate or drops with cluster adjustment.",
  "data_version": "Dataset freeze at the 2026-11-01 cut with the 2025-26 regular season complete (from 2026-04-13) and playoffs excluded. Record the graph and play-by-play versions and coverage checks before the test is run."
 }
}

